# Sudopod Server Implementation

## Overview

This specification defines the `createServer()` function that wraps any `Provider` implementation and exposes it as HTTP REST endpoints. The server is a thin translation layer - all business logic lives in the provider.

**Parent:** [[s-1u2m]] (Sudopod Provider Architecture)
**Depends on:** [[s-7gqg]] (Provider Interface Contract)

## Server Factory

```typescript
// src/server/index.ts

import express, { Express, Request, Response, NextFunction } from 'express';
import { Provider } from '../types';

/**
 * Creates an Express server that exposes a Provider as HTTP endpoints.
 * 
 * @param provider - Any Provider implementation (CoderProvider, etc.)
 * @param config - Server configuration
 * @returns Express app ready to listen()
 */
export function createServer(provider: Provider, config: ServerConfig): Express {
  const app = express();

  app.use(express.json());
  app.use(apiKeyAuth(config.apiKeys));

  const router = createRoutes(provider);
  app.use(config.basePath ?? '', router);

  app.use(errorHandler);

  return app;
}
```

