## Idempotent Operations

A key design principle is that **create() and resume() share internal logic** for the runtime operations, but **setup is only done once**:

```typescript
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// SETUP (create only) - runs once during workspace creation
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

private async applySetupConfig(workspaceId: string, setup: SetupConfig): Promise<void> {
  // Install agents
  if (setup.agents?.install?.length) {
    for (const agent of setup.agents.install) {
      await this.execInternal(workspaceId, `sudocode agent install ${agent}`);
    }
  }

  // Inject secrets
  if (setup.secrets) {
    for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(setup.secrets)) {
      await this.execInternal(workspaceId, `mkdir -p ~/.sudocode/secrets`);
      await this.execInternal(workspaceId, `echo "${value}" > ~/.sudocode/secrets/${key}`);
    }
  }

  // Configure models
  if (setup.models) {
    const config = JSON.stringify(setup.models);
    await this.execInternal(workspaceId, `echo '${config}' > ~/.sudocode/models.json`);
  }

  // Run setup script
  if (setup.setupScript) {
    await this.execInternal(workspaceId, setup.setupScript);
  }
}

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// RUNTIME (both create and resume) - runs every time
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

private async applyRuntimeConfig(workspaceId: string, runtime: RuntimeConfig): Promise<void> {
  const port = runtime.port ?? 3000;

  // 1. Ensure sudocode server is running
  const isRunning = await this.execInternal(workspaceId, `pgrep -f "sudocode.*--port ${port}"`);
  if (isRunning.exitCode !== 0) {
    await this.execInternal(workspaceId, `sudocode serve --port ${port} &`, { background: true });
    await this.waitForPort(workspaceId, port);
  }

  // 2. Ensure keepalive daemon is running (with current lifecycle settings)
  await this.ensureKeepaliveDaemon(workspaceId, runtime);

  // 3. Ensure port is forwarded
  await this.forwardPortInternal(workspaceId, port);
}
```

This means:
- `create()` calls `applySetupConfig()` once, then `applyRuntimeConfig()`
- `resume()` only calls `applyRuntimeConfig()` - setup is already done
- Calling `resume()` on an already-running workspace just bumps keepalive (idempotent)
- Lifecycle settings (idle timeout) can be adjusted on each resume

