## Error Handling

```typescript
class CoderApiError extends Error {
  constructor(
    public readonly status: number,
    public readonly body: string
  ) {
    super(`Coder API error (${status}): ${body}`);
    this.name = 'CoderApiError';
  }
}

// Common error cases:
// - 401 Unauthorized → Token invalid or expired
// - 403 Forbidden → No permission for operation
// - 404 Not Found → Workspace/template not found
// - 409 Conflict → Workspace name already exists
// - 500+ → Coder server error
```

