## Error Handling

```typescript
class CodespacesError extends Error {
  constructor(
    message: string,
    public readonly command: string,
    public readonly stderr: string,
    public readonly exitCode: number
  ) {
    super(message);
    this.name = 'CodespacesError';
  }
}

// Common error cases:
// - "gh: Not logged in" → throw with instructions to run `gh auth login`
// - "codespace not found" → throw WorkspaceNotFoundError
// - "you do not have permission" → throw PermissionError
// - Timeout waiting for state → throw TimeoutError
```

